Cell["\<\
h[k] returns the Hamiltonian matrix at sample k. samples may contain scalar \
parameters or momentum vectors.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->917745834,ExpressionUUID->"8704a9d4-3a06-d24d-8e4d-4ba7ad77bb40"],

Cell["\<\
The output has one row per retained band and one column per sample; \
eigenvalues are sorted separately at each sample, so bands are ordered by \
energy rather than tracked through crossings.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1008362305,ExpressionUUID->"de16d0e6-9384-5b49-b313-3333c6f13806"],

Cell["\<\
The {h, s} form solves the generalized eigenvalue problem with overlap matrix \
s[k].\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->1066079901,ExpressionUUID->"2872b302-ade8-f044-a515-f5e6a5cc1ada"],

Cell["\<\
n is passed to Eigenvalues; Eigenvalues options are accepted and Method -> \
\"Direct\" is supplied by the implementation.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->2023159276,ExpressionUUID->"80c5a645-9e97-d140-9d15-1866cff4e21c"]
}, Closed]],

